  "body": "This change adds atomic durable routing for partitioned stream DAGs: one payload, selected edge references, replay outcome, managed state and input cursor are persisted in one PostgreSQL transaction. It also prevents temporary launch-renewal failures from killing a healthy native flow.\n\nThe topology and routed store are implemented and independently checked. Public DAG start/execution and lifecycle remain fenced for NI2-012\u2013014. This integration is published and merged for the full CI run; epoch readiness remains 15%.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Implementation and validation</summary>\n\n- Typed sealed topology, shared worker-capacity admission, stable subscribers and forward/rebalance/broadcast/keyed routing.\n- Direct payload references, exact accepted-outcome replay, atomic cursor/state updates, contributor-aware EOF and paired PostgreSQL/SQLite migrations. Routed execution remains PostgreSQL-only.\n- Authenticated legacy-prefix refusal for DAG streams, preserving ordinary prefix behavior.\n- Renewal-only bounded retries and degraded monitoring, with stale-authority behavior preserved.\n\nIndependent verification passed: 38 PostgreSQL + 1 SQLite model cases; 23 migration cases on each backend; 5 PostgreSQL + 1 SQLite prefix cases; 17 checked server modules with zero type errors/warnings. Component SDK, packaging, planner and adapter checks are preserved in the evidence graph.\n\nThe renewal defect was reproduced on the old code. The corrected real-process scenario survived injected HTTP 500, lost acknowledgment and PostgreSQL lock timeout, recovered from cursor 200 to 201, retained four TaskRuns and released all slots. The architect personally repeated the injected scenario successfully.\n\nNormal commit and push hooks passed, including Mypy 1.14.1, Ruff and generated API/UI checks. The full hosted matrix and all 13 native process scenarios run against this integration; their results remain a separate gate.\n\n[Principal acceptance](https://github.com/Anacreonsystems/ariadne/blob/native-stream-storage/architecture/streaming-etl/evidence/native-epoch2-routed-server-2026-11-05/principal-v1/acceptance.json) \u00b7 [Publication evidence](https://github.com/Anacreonsystems/ariadne/blob/native-stream-storage/architecture/streaming-etl/evidence/native-epoch2-dag-routing-product-checkpoint-2026-11-05/index.json)\n\n</details>\n",
